class.description:
[PXTGI3D] can't read a [ShaderMaterial]'s glow: such a material needs a [code]pxtgi_emission[/code] [Color] in its metadata to light the scene off screen. This measures what a material actually emits by drawing it: each material on a tile of one HDR viewport, with no lights and no environment light, at a known exposure. The result includes everything the shader does to its emission (textures, tints, any multiplier it hides), so it's the value a tag should have. The editor's [b]Find Emissive Materials[/b] tool, on the [PXTGI3D] inspector, uses it.
Each material is read several times over about half a second: its glow is the mean of those readings, and one that changes over time (animated by [code]TIME[/code]) is flagged. The values are in the material's own units: nits with physical light units on.
[codeblock]
var meter := PXTGIEmissionMeter.new()
var found := PXTGIEmissionMeter.find_untagged(get_tree().edited_scene_root)
meter.measure(found.keys())
for result in await meter.finished:
    if result.luminance > 0.0:
        result.material.set_meta("pxtgi_emission", PXTGIEmissionMeter.emission_tag(result.glow))
[/codeblock]
